WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.180
Shine a laser at two narrow slits.

2
00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.500
On a screen beyond,
stripes of light appear.

3
00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:10.310
From those stripes, you can work
out the wavelength of the light.

4
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:14.580
Young saw two-slit stripes
like these in about 1801.

5
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:18.050
Yet physicists were slow
to accept what they showed.

6
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.070
How do you measure a
wavelength with two slits?

7
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.080
And why did it take so
long to be believed?

8
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:27.100
In this mission, you'll
set up the experiment:

9
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.570
a laser, a double slit and a
screen, in a darkened room.

10
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:35.200
Then you'll see how to make
the two slits coherent sources,

11
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.980
even without a laser.

12
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.250
Your mission: find out how
to measure the wavelength,

13
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.840
and why it took so long to be believed.
